From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0412-black-world-08-output-mean.patch

Source: 0412-black-world-08-output-mean.patch
mean channel

Run86 (Max Resolution, EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_SQUARE) logged "squares its E5B9G9R9 input" for the 1:1
network and scored 74 against run83's plain copy at 77, while in normal mode the same square took
run92's 60 to 90 outdoors to run89's 30 to 65. The stand-in's sampler logs the input's mean channel
(589 and 592 in those runs) but only the output's non-zero count and changes, so the logs cannot
say whether the squared output was darker than the plain one at 1:1.

The "output after blit" line now carries the same 3x10-bit mean as the input line. A squared copy
must read lower than its input; equal means the square never reached the output on that path.
Same sampling cadence (EDEN_NX2_SAMPLE_AT), no switch of its own.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
 src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp b/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
index fefb9ac2d6..0c66573bb6 100644
--- a/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
@@ -1532,15 +1532,20 @@ bool KeplerCompute::UpscaleInsteadOfNativeProgram() {
             rasterizer->FlushRegion(*device, size, VideoCommon::CacheType::All);
         }
         u32 nonzero{}, samples{}, changes{}, last{};
+        u64 sum{};
         for (u64 offset = 0; offset < size; offset += 4096 + 4) {
             const u32 word = memory_manager.Read<u32>(output->Address() + offset);
             ++samples;
             nonzero += word != 0;
             changes += word != last;
             last = word;
+            sum += (word & 0x3ff) + ((word >> 10) & 0x3ff) + ((word >> 20) & 0x3ff);
         }
-        LOG_INFO(HW_GPU, "Upscale fallback output after blit: {}/{} non-zero, {} changes", nonzero, samples,
-                 changes);
+        // The mean channel uses the input sampler's 3x10-bit reading, so the two compare: a copy
+        // that squares its input (EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_SQUARE) must read lower here than the input
+        // did, or the square never reached the output (run86: 74 against run83's 77 at 1:1).
+        LOG_INFO(HW_GPU, "Upscale fallback output after blit: {}/{} non-zero, {} changes, mean channel {}",
+                 nonzero, samples, changes, samples ? sum / (samples * 3) : 0);
     }
     // Debug: trace the draws that follow one upscale (EDEN_NX2_RT_TRACE_AFTER_UPSCALE).
     static const u32 trace_at = [] {
